The core that counts a tick gives time again only to the threads of its own core,
so a thread of another that waits for its account sits on the spent queue past the tick it has time again,
until its own core happens to count a tick; the release of every core lies ahead of the count.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a thread waits on another queue than its account says

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -501,7 +501,7 @@ static void tick_advance(uint32_t ticks)
     }
     for (uint32_t c = 0; c < CORES; c++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(CORES);
-        if (!tick_before(sched_ticks, cores[c].nearest_release)) {
+        if (c == core_index() && !tick_before(sched_ticks, cores[c].nearest_release)) {
             release(c);
         }
     }
